%N A401277 Irregular triangular array read by rows. T(n,k) is the number of ways to orient the edges of a simple labeled graph on [n] having exactly k edges so that there are no vertex descents then color the vertices with exactly n colors c1<c2<...<cn so that there are no color descents, 0<=k<=binomial(n,2), n>=0.
%C A401277 A descent in a labeled directed graph is an edge s->t such that s>t.
%C A401277 A color descent is an edge s->t such that the color of s is greater than the color of t.
%H A401277 Kassie Archer, Ira M. Gessel, Christina Graves, and Xuming Liang, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.01550">Counting acyclic and strong digraphs by descents</a>, arXiv:1909.01550 [math.CO], 20 Mar 2020.
%F A401277 Sum_{k>=0} Sum_{n>=0} T(n,k)*y^k*z^n/B(n) = 1/(1-z) where B(n) = Product_{i=1..n} Sum_{j=0..i-1} (1+y)^j.
%F A401277 T(n,binomial(n,2) = 1.
%F A401277 T(n,0) = n!.
%F A401277 T(n,1) = binomial(n,2)^2*(n-2)!.
%e A401277 Triangle begins:
%e A401277     1;
%e A401277     1;
%e A401277     2,   1;
%e A401277     6,   9,    5,    1;
%e A401277    24,  72,   98,   76,   35,    9,   1;
%e A401277   120, 600, 1450, 2200, 2299, 1717, 923, 351, 90, 14, 1;
%e A401277   ...
%e A401277 T(3,2) = 5 because we have: (1,c1)->(3,c3)<-(2,c2);  (1,c2)->(3,c3)<-(2,c1);
%e A401277  (2,c2)<-(1,c1)->(3,c3);  (2,c3)<-(1,c1)->(3,c2);   (1,c1)->(2,c2)->(3,c3);
%t A401277 nn = 7; B[n_] := FunctionExpand[QFactorial[n, (1 + y)]]; Map[CoefficientList[#, y] &, Table[B[n], {n, 0, nn}] CoefficientList[Series[1/(1 - z), {z, 0, nn}], z]]
%Y A401277 Cf. A005329 (row sums), A401320.
